# Keep documentation in sync

When changing documented Chili behavior, public APIs, configuration, defaults,
examples, or known limitations, update the relevant documentation in both this
repository and `/home/jshinonome/Workspace/purple-chili.github.io` in the same task.

- Read the documentation repository's instructions and Git status before editing;
  preserve unrelated changes.
- Match examples, signatures, defaults, return values, and limitations to the
  implementation. For example, dataframe operations belong in
  `docs/built-in-functions/df.md`, writer behavior in `io.md`, and configuration
  in `config.md` in the documentation repository.
- Use the documentation repository's existing build workflow to validate edits.
- When committing and pushing an authorized documentation sync, include the
  corresponding changes in both repositories and report both commits.
- If the companion repository is unavailable, state which documentation remains
  unsynchronized rather than claiming the update is complete.
